      "date": "2026-11-22",
      "title": "Microsoft Entra Connect Health, Rackspace Spot and GPGME flaws",
      "description": "Microsoft confirms attackers read tenant metadata through a flaw in Entra Connect Health, and Rackspace Spot customers are told to rotate Kubernetes secrets after a breach. Also covered: a critical GPGME flaw, four actively exploited flaws added to CISA's catalog, AI router key theft research, a Meta Muse demonstration and a MoEngage vendor breach.",
      "show_notes_html": "<p>Microsoft confirms attackers read tenant metadata through a flaw in Entra Connect Health, and Rackspace Spot customers are told to rotate Kubernetes secrets after a breach. Also covered: a critical GPGME flaw, four actively exploited flaws added to CISA&#x27;s catalog, AI router key theft research, a Meta Muse demonstration and a MoEngage vendor breach.</p><p>Stories covered:</p><ul><li>Entra Connect Health flaw exploited to read tenant data &mdash; Sources: <a href=\"https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/microsoft-entra-connect-health-flaw-exploited-to-steal-tenant-data/\">BleepingComputer</a></li><li>Rackspace Spot breach exposed customer Kubernetes secrets &mdash; Sources: <a href=\"https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/rackspace-spot-breach-let-hackers-access-customer-kubernetes-secrets/\">BleepingComputer</a></li><li>Researchers say AI routers broke privacy and stole keys &mdash; Sources: <a href=\"https://www.techmeme.com/261121/p10#a261121p10\">Techmeme</a></li><li>Critical GPGME flaw could expose application data &mdash; Sources: <a href=\"https://thehackernews.com/2026/11/gnupg-warns-critical-gpgme-flaw-could.html\">The Hacker News</a>, <a href=\"https://lists.gnupg.org/pipermail/gnupg-announce/2026q4/000517.html\">Hacker News</a></li><li>CISA adds four exploited flaws, including VMware vCenter &mdash; Sources: <a href=\"https://thehackernews.com/2026/11/hackers-exploit-critical-vmware-cisco.html\">The Hacker News</a></li><li>Researchers hijack Meta Muse AI agent with a malicious page &mdash; Sources: <a href=\"https://thehackernews.com/2026/11/a-single-malicious-webpage-let.html\">The Hacker News</a></li><li>MoEngage breached through a compromised vendor account &mdash; Sources: <a href=\"https://inc42.com/buzz/now-moengage-suffers-cybersecurity-attack-due-to-compromised-third-party-vendor/\">Inc42</a></li></ul>",
