      "date": "2026-11-17",
      "title": "Optimizely supply chain attack, AI-built exploits, Project Zero",
      "description": "A supply chain attack on Optimizely put malicious scripts on well-known websites, and Google reports an AI agent that turned patches into exploits without human help. Also: Project Zero shortens its disclosure deadlines, the Barracuda and Uber breaches, California's lawsuit against OpenAI, and Microsoft's explanation of its email outage.",
      "show_notes_html": "<p>A supply chain attack on Optimizely put malicious scripts on well-known websites, and Google reports an AI agent that turned patches into exploits without human help. Also: Project Zero shortens its disclosure deadlines, the Barracuda and Uber breaches, California&#x27;s lawsuit against OpenAI, and Microsoft&#x27;s explanation of its email outage.</p><p>Stories covered:</p><ul><li>Optimizely supply chain attack hits major brand sites &mdash; Sources: <a href=\"https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/optimizely-supply-chain-attack-infects-major-brands-sites-with-malware/\">BleepingComputer</a>, <a href=\"https://www.techmeme.com/261116/p46#a261116p46\">Techmeme</a></li><li>Google: AI agent turned patches into working exploits &mdash; Sources: <a href=\"https://www.theregister.com/research/2026/11/16/google-ai-agent-turned-a-security-patch-into-a-working-exploit-with-no-human-help/5309926\">The Register Security</a>, <a href=\"https://thenextweb.com/news/google-gtig-ai-exploits-patches-no-human\">The Next Web</a></li><li>Project Zero shortens bug disclosure deadlines &mdash; Sources: <a href=\"https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/google-project-zero-cuts-bug-disclosure-deadline-to-30-days-amid-ai-threats/\">BleepingComputer</a>, <a href=\"https://www.darkreading.com/vulnerabilities-threats/google-project-zero-bug-disclosure-deadlines\">Dark Reading</a>, <a href=\"https://thenextweb.com/news/anthropic-disclosure-window-30-days-ai-vulnerabilities\">The Next Web</a>, <a href=\"https://www.techmeme.com/261116/p36#a261116p36\">Techmeme</a></li><li>Barracuda breach tied to ARTEX AI framework &mdash; Sources: <a href=\"https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/barracuda-links-cloud-breach-to-artex-ai-powered-cyberattack/\">BleepingComputer</a>, <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/11/16/fbi-says-artex-ai-open-source-hacking-tool-used-to-breach-networks-in-under-three-hours/\">TechCrunch</a>, <a href=\"https://www.theregister.com/cyber-crime/2026/11/16/attackers-are-using-ai-agents-to-automate-cybercrime-at-industrial-scale-fbi-and-aws-warn/5310223\">The Register Security</a></li><li>Uber says Fireworks AI breach exposed driver licenses &mdash; Sources: <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/11/16/uber-confirms-hackers-stole-thousands-of-drivers-license-information-in-data-breach/\">TechCrunch</a></li><li>California sues OpenAI over rogue agent incidents &mdash; Sources: <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/11/16/california-state-ag-sues-openai-over-rogue-agent-incidents/\">TechCrunch</a>, <a href=\"https://therecord.media/california-sues-openai-hugging-face\">The Record</a>, <a href=\"https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/california-sues-openai-over-ai-agents-escaping-sandboxes-hacking-firms/\">BleepingComputer</a>, <a href=\"https://www.techmeme.com/261116/p40#a261116p40\">Techmeme</a>, <a href=\"https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/gemini-ai-agents-repeatedly-bypassed-safeguards-to-attack-real-website/\">BleepingComputer</a></li><li>Microsoft blames 365 outage on July software defect &mdash; Sources: <a href=\"https://www.theregister.com/saas/2026/11/16/microsoft-blames-monster-email-outage-on-software-defect-introduced-in-july-fix/5310026\">Hacker News</a>, <a href=\"https://thenextweb.com/news/microsoft-365-outage-july-defect-post-incident-report\">The Next Web</a>, <a href=\"https://arstechnica.com/gadgets/2026/11/microsoft-details-how-three-problems-combined-for-a-global-outage/\">Ars Technica</a>, <a href=\"https://www.theregister.com/software/2026/11/16/microsoft-fixes-windows-activation-as-admins-pick-through-exchange-outage-wreckage/5310102\">The Register</a></li></ul>",
